data.content:
Yes! C# fully supports `stackalloc` with native-sized integers. Both `Span<nint>` and `Span<nuint>` work:

```csharp
Span<nint>  nints  = stackalloc nint[5];
Span<nuint> nuints = stackalloc nuint[3];
```

On this 64-bit system, each element is 8 bytes. The feature works because `nint`/`nuint` (introduced in C# 9) are unmanaged types, which is the requirement for `stackalloc`.
